cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these materials in published research or educational curricula, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "Public Lands Institute — OER Learning Objects: Michigan/Ohio Fieldwork Series"
abstract: >
  Open Educational Resource modules documenting industrial-ecological land use history
  and Indigenous displacement at four Great Lakes and Great Black Swamp sites: Eagle Island
  Marsh, Pointe Mouillee State Game Area, Howard Marsh Metropark, and Oak Openings Preserve
  Metropark. Each module integrates forensic ecological reporting with Shadow History
  methodology, centering Potawatomi, Wyandot, and Ottawa land tenure prior to treaty
  dispossession. Primary source photography is black-and-white large-format field documentation.
