references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Treaty of Detroit (1807)"
    notes: "Ceded Wyandot, Ottawa, Potawatomi, and Ojibwe land claims in southeastern Michigan, including the Lake Erie shoreline."
  - type: generic
    title: "Treaty of Maumee Rapids (1817)"
    notes: "Ceded northwestern Ohio territorial claims of Wyandot, Ottawa, Seneca, and Shawnee nations."
  - type: generic
    title: "Treaty of Chicago (1833)"
    notes: "Ceded Ottawa and Potawatomi claims in northeastern Indiana and northwestern Ohio, including Oak Openings region."
  - type: generic
    title: "Indian Removal Act (1830)"
    notes: "Federal legislation authorizing forced removal of Indigenous nations east of the Mississippi."
